From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antheas Kapenekakis <lkml@antheas.dev>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 20:10:02 +0200
Subject: hid: steam: retain controller while steam is open

Currently, when a hidraw reader interacts with hid-steam, the kernel
driver closes the evdev node for the driver. This eliminates _some_
potential bugs with games seeing two controllers, although Steam handles
this perfectly fine for the myriad of other controllers. However, this
stops other applications from reading controller inputs, such as
Handheld Daemon, so we can no longer intercept the controller.
Therefore, remove the muting and unregistering that happens when Steam
connects to the controller. Keep the gates that controll sensor output
and lizard mode, such that Steam or another hid client still controls
device behavior.
---
 drivers/hid/hid-steam.c | 19 ++++---------------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-steam.c b/drivers/hid/hid-steam.c
