From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antheas Kapenekakis <lkml@antheas.dev>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 14:44:22 +0200
Subject: platform/x86: Add Lenovo WMI lighting driver

Lenovo Legion Go firmware exposes the power button light through the
Lighting WMI interface. Depending on the firmware, it provides a combined
runtime and suspend control, independent power and standby controls, or all
three controls aliased to one EC setting.

Add a driver which detects the implemented layout using read-only status
queries. Prefer the combined control when it is available so that aliased
firmware exposes one platform::power LED; otherwise expose independent
platform::power and platform::standby LEDs. Retain both LED states at
shutdown.

Document the interface and the combined-control semantics.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Antheas Kapenekakis <lkml@antheas.dev>
---
