Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:42:03 +0200
Subject: wifi: auth12k: gate RCU modifications on unload

While testing a Qualcomm laptop with missing WiFi firmware, unloading
the driver caused it to oops, bringing down the system. This is caused
by the early failure leaving dangling pointers. Therefore, check for
non-null before assigning the pointers and removing them, fixing the
crash.

Assisted-by: Codex:sol-6
Signed-off-by: Antheas Kapenekakis <lkml@antheas.dev>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c
index 779529d189f8abe94153f72a744593ad118e0a04..119c84922b6f800c46e9bb18a32c817e0f9df769 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c
@@ -843,13 +843,16 @@ void ath12k_dp_pdev_free(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ab->num_radios; i++) {
 		ar = ab->pdevs[i].ar;
-		rcu_assign_pointer(dp->dp_pdevs[ar->pdev_idx], NULL);
+		if (ar)
+			rcu_assign_pointer(dp->dp_pdevs[ar->pdev_idx], NULL);
 	}
 
 	synchronize_rcu();
 
-	for (i = 0; i < ab->num_radios; i++)
-		ath12k_dp_rx_pdev_free(ab, i);
+	for (i = 0; i < ab->num_radios; i++) {
+		if (ab->pdevs[i].ar)
+			ath12k_dp_rx_pdev_free(ab, i);
+	}
 }
 
 void ath12k_dp_pdev_pre_alloc(struct ath12k *ar)
