From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antheas Kapenekakis <lkml@antheas.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:00:58 +0200
Subject: platform: arm64: add Galaxy Book4 Edge EC platform driver

The Galaxy Book4 Edge devices use the ENE-KB9058 IC as their main EC
platform driver. It provides battery information, controls power
profiles, and keyboard backlight. In addition, a secondary I2C node
provides special button information, specifically the fan and keyboard
backlight keys. Those keys initially produce HID vendor reports, which
then route through I2C to reach the EC driver in Windows.

Therefore, add a fully functional EC driver for the platform,
implementing platform profiles, keyboard backlight, and battery
information. Wire the secondary I2C to this driver, so backlight and fan
key notifications route through it and update the device state directly.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Antheas Kapenekakis <lkml@antheas.dev>
