From: Antheas Kapenekakis <lkml@antheas.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:33:44 +0200
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: Split Galaxy Book4 Edge X1E board description

Keep the shared regulators, codec, EC, wireless devices and pinctrl in a
SoC-independent Galaxy Book4 Edge include. Move the X1E-specific display,
speakers, USB wiring and firmware paths into an X1E include that selects
the Hamoa SoC and PMICs.

Point the existing 14-inch and 16-inch leaves at the X1E include so the
common core can also support an X1P derivative.

Validation: both base and EL2 DTBs build; all compiled hardware properties
of the 14-inch and 16-inch boards are unchanged by the split.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
