From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antheas Kapenekakis <lkml@antheas.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:39:48 +0200
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: galaxy-book4-edge: enable USB-A only on 16-inch
 model

The 14-inch Galaxy Book4 Edge has no USB-A port, but inherits the
multiport USB controller and PHY enablement from the shared X1E device
tree. On this model, xHCI setup times out with -ETIMEDOUT after about
17 seconds, delaying boot.

Move the multiport controller and PHY configuration into the 16-inch
DTS. The 14-inch model now inherits their disabled status from the SoC
device tree, while its two USB-C controllers remain enabled. The
15-inch model has separate USB-A configuration and is unaffected.

Build the 14-, 15- and 16-inch DTBs and verify the resulting controller
and PHY status properties. Hardware boot validation is pending.
