From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:13:25 +0700
Subject: Input: rsinput - add AYN and Retroid Pocket UART gamepad driver

Add a serdev driver for the gamepad microcontroller found in AYN and
Retroid Pocket handhelds. The MCU is attached to a UART at 115200 baud
and reports the buttons, two analog sticks and two triggers in
periodic status frames.

On probe the driver powers the MCU from its vdd supply, sequences the
optional enable, reset and boot GPIOs, requests the firmware version
and configures the report parameters. Frames are validated by
checksum, with resynchronisation on the frame header. The MCU is
powered down on suspend and re-initialised on resume, dropping reports
for a short settling time.

The input device name and ID come from the gamepad-name, gamepad-bus,
gamepad-vid, gamepad-pid and gamepad-rev properties. Per-board tuning
is described in DT.

The tuning properties follow the ROCKNIX rsinput driver by Philippe
Simons and Jacob Cook.

Signed-off-by: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
---
 drivers/input/joystick/Kconfig   |  11 +
 drivers/input/joystick/Makefile  |   1 +
 drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c | 559 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 571 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c

