From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:23:30 +0700
Subject: leds: Add driver for HEROIC HTR3212

The HEROIC HTR3212 is a 12-channel LED driver with 8-bit PWM brightness
control, configured over I2C. It is used for the joystick RGB lights.

Each DT child node describes one output channel and is registered as a
separate LED class device. Brightness is written to the channel's PWM
register and latched with the update register.

On probe the driver enables the vdd supply, releases the chip from
shutdown through the SDB GPIO, resets the registers, enables all
outputs and sets the PWM output frequency. The chip is powered down on
suspend and re-initialised on resume. LEDs are blanked over suspend
unless the controller node has the always-on property.

Signed-off-by: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
---
 drivers/leds/Kconfig        |  12 ++
 drivers/leds/Makefile       |   1 +
 drivers/leds/leds-htr3212.c | 362 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 375 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/leds/leds-htr3212.c

diff --git a/drivers/leds/Kconfig b/drivers/leds/Kconfig
index ed7e27ffae85596b7d95d09651ba29fde475c3f5..affb0bb04b672a6a1cdceed7dac88c756fc34378 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/leds/Kconfig
@@ -227,6 +227,18 @@ config LEDS_EL15203000
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
 	  will be called leds-el15203000.
 
+config LEDS_HTR3212
+	tristate "LED support for HEROIC HTR3212"
+	depends on LEDS_CLASS && I2C && OF
+	select REGMAP_I2C
+	help
+	  This option enables support for the HEROIC HTR3212 12-channel
+	  LED controller with 8-bit PWM brightness control, connected
+	  over I2C.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
+	  will be called leds-htr3212.
+
 config LEDS_TURRIS_OMNIA
 	tristate "LED support for CZ.NIC's Turris Omnia"
 	depends on LEDS_CLASS_MULTICOLOR
