Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:06:26 +0700
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: add common dtsi for QCS8550 Retroid Pocket devices

The Retroid Pocket 6 and Retroid Pocket Nova are handheld gaming
devices based on the Qualcomm QCS8550 that share most of their
hardware. Add a common dtsi describing it:

- PMIC regulators, power and volume keys, RTC
- GPU, video encoder/decoder and display subsystem with DisplayPort
  alt mode over USB-C
- USB-C with role switching and orientation detection via pmic-glink
- UFS storage and microSD card slot
- Wi-Fi (WCN7850 over PCIe) and Bluetooth
- Audio: AW88166 speaker amplifiers on Primary MI2S, WCD9385 headset
  codec with headset jack and on-board digital microphones
- Gamepad controller over UART (RSInput)
- PWM fan driven by the CPU and GPU thermal zones
- Debug UART

The display panel, touchscreen and joystick lights differ per board
and are described in the board files.

