From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:10:06 +0700
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: add common dtsi for Eliza Retroid Pocket devices

Add a common dtsi for Retroid Pocket handhelds based on the Qualcomm
Eliza platform, describing their shared hardware:

- PMIC regulators, power and volume keys, lid hall sensor
- GPU, video encoder/decoder and display subsystem with DisplayPort
  alt mode over USB-C
- USB-C with role switching and orientation detection via pmic-glink
- UFS storage and microSD card slot
- Wi-Fi (WCN7750 on the WPSS remoteproc) and Bluetooth
- Audio: AW88166 speaker amplifiers on Primary MI2S, ES8326 headset
  codec on Quaternary MI2S with headset jack, and on-board digital
  microphones on the VA macro
- AW86927 haptics
- Gamepad controller over UART (RSInput)
- Charging and status LEDs on the PM7550 LPG
- PWM fan driven by the CPU and GPU thermal zones
- Debug UART

The display panels and touchscreens differ per board and are described
in the board files.

Signed-off-by: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
---
 .../dts/qcom/eliza-retroidpocket-common.dtsi  | 1370 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 1370 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/eliza-retroidpocket-common.dtsi

